# What a share-link holder sees: the set's name, when the link stops
# working, and the accessions that have been put on it.
#
# Its own template rather than anything the set's members are served, and
# this is where the two differ rather than where they happen to agree.
# There is no roster here, no conversation, no submission, no owner and no
# curation status — a reviewer is being shown some records, not a
# collaboration and not DDBJ's handling of it.
#
# The rows are resolved through the set every time (ReviewerAccess#
# shared_rows), so a submission taken out of the set is gone from here
# without anything having to remember to remove it.
{
  name:       @access.set.name,
  expires_at: @access.expires_at,

  accessions: @rows.map {|row|
    facts = AccessionFacts.for(row)

    {
      accession: facts.accession,
      db:        facts.db,
      name:      facts.name,
      details:   facts.details
    }
  }
}
